# Code owners for ask-me-anything.
#
# GitHub requests a review from the owner of every file a pull request
# touches, and `main` has "Require review from Code Owners" enabled.
#
# SINGLE-MAINTAINER WARNING: GitHub does not let an author approve their
# own pull request. While @hongchenme is the only owner named here, every
# PR they open needs a second reviewer added below, or the branch
# protection on `main` relaxed. Adding this file makes that rule bite --
# before it existed, no file had an owner, so the rule matched nothing.

# Default owner for anything not matched more specifically below.
*                           @hongchenme

# The escape boundary, and the reason this file is not just `*`.
# `__ama_sq`'s output is placed back into the user's interactive shell
# buffer and then executed, so a flaw here turns a typed question into
# executed code (RISK-02). It is property-tested against the real shell
# rather than a reimplementation -- see tests/shell_functions.rs. The
# whole-branch review found a test here that passed against a hook doing
# no escaping at all. Changes in this directory deserve the closest look
# of anything in the repository.
/crates/ama/src/shell/      @hongchenme

# The install path. `install.sh` and `ama setup` edit a user's `.bashrc`
# or `.zshrc` and create the `@@` alias; it is the first thing a new user
# runs, and two defects here have already shipped and been caught in
# review (an init guard that aborted the caller's rc, and an rc whose
# hook never loaded in a login shell).
/install.sh                 @hongchenme
/crates/ama/src/cli.rs      @hongchenme

# CI and release plumbing. `release.yml` is generated by `dist generate`;
# hand-editing it makes `dist generate --check` fail.
/.github/workflows/         @hongchenme
/dist-workspace.toml        @hongchenme
